{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0069","billNumberShort":"H.B. 69","billNumberLong":"HB0069S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0792","shortTitle":"Drinking Water Restructuring Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"ALBRECR","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Albrecht, Carl R.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses violations of the Safe Drinking Water Act.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>creates and modifies terms;<hr><ltbullet>allows a court to:<hr><ltbullet1>appoint a receiver for a supplier of a public water system to implement a corrective or remedial action for a violation of the Safe Drinking Water Act (SDWA) or compliance order; and<hr><ltbullet1>require a violator to divest ownership of the public water system to ensure long-term compliance with SDWA;<hr><ltbullet>requires the director of the Division of Drinking Water to report to a legislative committee if the director brings a civil action that may result in a receivership or divestment for a public water system supplier; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Ryan C. Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"PFMTABVHMG","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-22 16:03:34.653","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-22 16:03:34.667","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCod